{
  "dom_id": "step-e12715",
  "name": "Example: Writing Biconditionals as Conditionals",
  "problem": "Express the following statement as a conjunction of implications.\n\n$$\n\\neg P \\Leftrightarrow Q\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $A \\Leftrightarrow B$ is true if $A\\Rightarrow B$ **and** $B\\Rightarrow A.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $A \\Leftrightarrow B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\neg P \\Leftrightarrow Q \\equiv (\\neg P \\Rightarrow Q) \\land (Q \\Rightarrow \\neg P).\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
